From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: build the AROS target and detect its data natively

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: fastfetch builds for Linux, BSD, macOS, Windows, Haiku and others,
not for AROS, which has a POSIX C library (posixc) but no /proc, /sys,
dlopen, poll, fnmatch or user accounts, AmigaDOS paths and its own APIs
for everything fastfetch reports.
Solution: an AROS branch in CMakeLists.txt (features that need missing
facilities off, link through the SDK's own GCC driver, no full strip) and
*_aros.c backends that ask AROS itself: exec, dos, graphics, intuition,
locale, processor.resource, timer.device, bsdsocket.library (opened by the
Local IP module only, so the program starts without a TCP/IP stack).
Paths follow AmigaDOS (ENVARC:, ENV:, PROGDIR:; never "Vol:/file").
Terminal capabilities come from the Limpet SDK's presentation and identity
queries on the actual output handle; every stdout write passes one filter
for Amiga pen colours and Latin-1 consoles. Modules without a reliable
source report "Not supported on AROS"; missing data stays missing.
ABIv11 gets small replacements for POSIX calls its C library lacks.
Scope: AROS only. Upstream files are touched only behind __AROS__ / the
AROS CMake branch: disk folder patterns use dos.library matching and ';'
as separator (':' is part of every AmigaDOS path), io_unix.c has no poll,
netif.h includes the BSD headers AROS needs first, the interactive
--gen-config needs a terminal fastfetch cannot query on AROS and is off.
Upstream-Status: AROS-specific; could be offered upstream as a platform
once it has users. Needs the Limpet SDK 0.6.0 sources (vendor/limpet-sdk).
Verification: built for aros-x86_64-abiv11-pc, aros-x86_64-abiv1-pc and
aros-aarch64-abiv1-raspi; tests/aros/smoke.script and console runs on pool
v1-1, v11-1 and rpi-1 (2026-10-27); host tests in tests/test_port.py.
Removal: when upstream fastfetch supports AROS.
